@@ -0,0 +1,51 @@
+# Configurable native saved-life research profile
+
+This is the separate `research_catalog_v1` profile for the **same** `evaluate_saved_life_retention --experiment-manifest ROOT CURRENT OUTPUT MANIFEST` entrypoint. It is not the frozen R41 promotion card and cannot emit promotion authority. Keep the deployed v1 binary (588b6094…), frozen control proof, rubric, base and state unchanged.
+
+## Source and study contract
+
+Apply the source-only overlay on the exact source reconstructed by `docs/r41-saved-life/restore_source.py` at `f466b83791cccb97568e6f718b92b052999cfb2b` (anchor `c5d250178cb70a10f99f78ebcc974e0ad5533b41`). It does not apply directly to the historical unoverlaid `crates/` snapshot. The OS/toolchain/driver must be qualified independently; an unqualified binary must never be given a research admission file. Do not replace the active v1 binary or copy any private checkpoint into Git.
+
+The operator supplies three bounded, exact local documents in each admitted arm: `operator-research-admission.v1.json`, `research-catalog.v1.json`, `research-rubric.v1.json`. Admission is a separate operator-provided digest pin, not embedded in a contender or allowed inline in the manifest. Example shape, with **non-operational placeholders**:
+
+```json
+{
+  "schema": "qualia.saved_life.operator_research_admission.v1",
+  "catalog_sha256": "<exact catalog bytes>",
+  "rubric_sha256": "<exact external rubric bytes>",
+  "evaluator_sha256": "<qualified research ELF bytes>",
+  "admitted_case_ids": ["contact-hot-left", "contact-same-hot-harmless-left", "contact-warm-edible-left", "reach-food", "reach-inert"]
+}
+```
+
+The manifest names one admitted case, a pinned caller Current, the sole living owner, common expected world seed and evaluation nonce. The catalog describes only integer-unit body-relative native `Hazard`, `Obstacle`, and `Food` placements and required physical opening contacts. Coordinates, radii, dose, heat, nutritional content, counts, geometry and horizons are bounded. Unknown fields and overlapping or ambiguous geometry fail ahead of even the Current path check. No arbitrary commands, rewards, target IDs, brain data, policy inputs, terrain mutation, placeholder sensors, or inline runner settings are accepted. The rubric bytes are hashed but not parsed by the simulator; labels/slots are kept in observers, not creature inputs.
+
+Native materialization is transactional on a disposable saved world. It does not reposition the body, normalize the saved scene, clear prior experiences, or change the retained sampler, time, optimizer or learned state. It succeeds only if the actual quiet, flat, local opening permits the declared data. The runner measures actual contacts, paid decisions, health/pain/injury, target clearance and real ownership/nourishment. A host that cannot realize the declared physical opening is **incompatible**, not a losing creature. Terrain edits are deliberately not part of this first operation set.
+
+`contact-*` includes mirror hot harmful/same-hot same-kind harmless/warm edible conditions. Score escape only after paid, genuinely outward Flee on the same target followed by sustained clearance under the frozen injury cap. Warm Food needs real same-target custody and ingestion. `reach-food`/`reach-inert` is a second data-only fixture with an entirely different opening geometry and contact schedule, using the same binary/ABI and ordinary control flow. No pass, gain or generalization is claimed until an independently accepted native run.
+
+## Inputs and exact command
+
+The normal `complete_saved_life` input is an **exact native Current** and preserves actual history. Its independent file hash is required for each arm. Equal source seed and trial settings are checked; genuinely different hashes are called an *independent saved-life comparison*, not a brain-only causal experiment, even when seeds match. Saved sampling streams are not replaced to create cosmetic matching. For a standalone canonical `FoundationWeightAsset`, provide the asset SHA **and an explicit compatible full native host Current**. The native canonical decoder and existing safe N2048 calibration transaction admit only exact, reconstructible assets on legal inherited coordinates. An incompatible topology, protected stage/speech difference, unsupported provenance, or unrecognized file format is refused, not silently converted to a founder or mislabeled as acquired history. Native installation cannot write the host’s mutable acquired rails. A same-host asset comparison should use the same source Current and owner in both arms. It is still not v1 promotion evidence.
+
+From the candidate checkout, device-free plan:
+
+```sh
+python3 scripts/research_saved_life_catalog.py \
+  --catalog docs/research-saved-life/research-catalog.v1.json \
+  --rubric docs/research-saved-life/research-rubric.v1.json \
+  --admission "$ADMISSION" --admission-sha256 "$ADMISSION_SHA" --evaluator "$RESEARCH_ELF" \
+  --world-seed "$COMMON_WORLD_SEED" --nonce "$COMMON_NONCE" --case contact-hot-left \
+  --a-current "$CURRENT_A" --a-sha256 "$CURRENT_A_SHA" --a-owner "$OWNER_A" \
+  --b-current "$CURRENT_B" --b-sha256 "$CURRENT_B_SHA" --b-owner "$OWNER_B"
+```
+
+For A5 after the active lease clears, add `--execute --output "$NEW_PRIVATE_RUN" --lease "$EXISTING_SHARED_NATIVE_LEASE" --lavapipe-so "$PINNED_LAVAPIPE_SO" --lavapipe-icd "$PINNED_LAVAPIPE_ICD"`. For each `a` and `b` also add `--a-reopen "$ACCEPTED_A" --a-reopen-sha256 "$ACCEPTED_A_SHA" --a-reopen-process "$PROCESS_A" --a-reopen-process-sha256 "$PROCESS_A_SHA" --a-reopen-raw "$RAW_NATIVE_A"` and the corresponding B flags. Those are **real independent separate-process zero-cut approvals** on the exact new binary using the existing restore-only protocol, never derived from the plan or generated by this wrapper. For an explicit Foundation arm, add its `--a-foundation "$FOUNDATION_A" --a-foundation-sha256 "$FOUNDATION_A_SHA"` optionally. Set case to the corresponding admitted foils and `reach-food`/`reach-inert` with the same executable. Use a new output directory for each paired case. Only plans run without the signed-off native admission, lease and resource floor.
+
+## Qualification order (not yet executed)
+
+1. Run `PYTHONDONTWRITEBYTECODE=1 python3 scripts/test_research_saved_life_catalog.py -v` (device-free). Build the normal production closure and run the bounded CLI harness with `cargo test --frozen --offline --release -p alife_game_app --features foundation-training,gpu-tests --bin evaluate_saved_life_retention`. Its actual world allocator regression adds two real props with neutral local names, with the first default name already occupied by a host prop. The pinned production-only source closure deliberately omits unrelated experimental assets required by `cargo test --lib`. On the compiled executable verify a malformed admitted placement fails before touching a deliberately nonexistent Current, and genuine v1 control/receipt behavior matches the old proof before any native claim. Keep the old v1 production promotion evaluator pinned regardless.
+2. Under the existing shared lease, produce independent same-binary zero-cut proofs for two actual complete Currents with the same world seed. A may be R41 or another known complete host. B must come from a separately documented non-R41 branch/organism, not a weight edit or clone of R41; select an already held compatible independent Current, or arrange one to be retained through the ordinary same-individual production checkpoint pathway first. Verify both hosts meet the same local world constraints. Stage no nonexistent checkpoint as a pass.
+3. Run one case per family and their foils on both Currents through exactly this binary and argument path. Report input, catalog, admission, case/fixture, rubric, evaluator, process, native receipt, native rows, and effective Current hashes. Valid control and no measured gain is still a real result; absent layout/device/source or corrupt evidence is not biological failure. If the study is selected to grow, repeat the existing left/right conditions from the frozen catalog and separately authorize any additional ecology or terrain operation. Keep research and promotion artifacts separate.
+
+No Rust build, real native execution or acceptance has occurred in this isolated source branch workspace.
